# English captions (seconds in the ORIGINAL recording). *word* = shown in gold. Review by hand before rendering.
CAPTIONS = [
    (1.51, 32.33, "A'udhu billahi min ash-shaytan ir-rajeem. Bismillah ir-Rahman ir-Raheem. It has started to rain. How wonderful — MashaAllah. May Allah show all of you."),
    (33.05, 67.03, "And may you know that the dars here can also be seen. What is it? Kashf — it opens. Here, by reading the teachings of the Prophet ﷺ, kashf comes too. Do you understand? And from above, ilqa — inspiration — also opens. This is Allah's grace."),
    (69.43, 110.99, "A'udhu billah, Bismillah. In Haqeeqat-e-Bai'at, Huzoor Shams-ul-Mufassireen, Khadim-ul-Quran, Bahr-ul-Uloom Hazrat Muhammad Abdul Qadeer Siddiqui Hasrat Rahmatullah Alaih, Professor and former Head of the Department of Theology, Osmania University — published by the Hasrat Academy long ago; this is its third printing."),
    (110.99, 135.93, "Hazrat writes: “Every Muslim man and woman should do istighfar — so why is a murshid needed for istighfar?”"),
    (137.59, 191.33, "Such objections and questions are answered in the Qur'an. Now see, this is written on a verse of the Qur'an: “If, when they had wronged themselves, they had come to you and asked Allah's forgiveness, and the Messenger had asked forgiveness for them, they would have found Allah Accepting of repentance, Most Merciful.” (an-Nisa 4:64)"),
    (191.33, 238.67, "It is clear from this that asking forgiveness on one's own is not enough; the prayer of one whose heart is enlightened should also be sought — just as the Prophet ﷺ himself would pray for their forgiveness."),
    (238.67, 261.07, "“May Allah forgive their sins.” Becoming a murid begins with istighfar: the murshid prays for forgiveness for him, and there is hope that it will be accepted."),
    (262.07, 316.87, "Just think: love for the sake of Allah. It is a very important thing; it is in the hadith: for those who love one another for Allah's sake, pulpits of light will be set up — a station so high that the prophets will say, “Oh, what a station!”"),
    (316.87, 375.57, "Think with a calm heart: why does the murid love his murshid? He loves him for the sake of Allah. Love for Allah's sake is what is between the two. Oh! With Allah, the matter of love goes so far!"),
    (378.01, 409.65, "Don't you know? “A person is with the one he loves.” And you are with the one you love."),
    (410.01, 429.17, "There is an address in this: someone came and asked, and he was told — the Companion was told — “A person will be with the one he loves.”"),
    (429.95, 454.75, "And it is in the Holy Qur'an: even if the children fall short in deeds, Allah joins them with their parents in Paradise. (at-Tur 52:21)"),
    (457.42, 473.58, "Who are these murids? They are spiritual children. Wow! InshaAllah, the murids will be joined with their master."),
    (476.28, 491.80, "Wow! Khwaja ya Sarkar, Khwaja ya Sarkar, Ghaus-e-Pak Sarkar! SubhanAllah, MashaAllah."),
    (492.47, 503.14, "What is being read now is not just for sitting and listening — you have to act on it at once. That is why you are rushing forward, and I joined you at once."),
    (507.04, 522.22, "So what am I doing? I am meeting you, but I am giving my hand to Qadeer Piya. I see myself there. Why are you looking at me? I am looking there, not at you — at my master."),
    (524.44, 540.26, "MashaAllah — wow, wow! Everyone has joined hands. MashaAllah. May you live long!"),
    (540.92, 568.18, "Now what are you doing? You have started meeting me — and through me, Qadeer Piya. He is my master, so you are happy that you met our master. He is the master of the master — the Dada, Dada Peer. That is why we give it attention."),
    (568.62, 580.00, "Who are these murids? Spiritual children. InshaAllah, the murids will be joined with their master; they will rise with him."),
    (583.00, 607.20, "They will rise with him from the grave. As soon as they rise they will say: “Where is my master?” and they will go to their master."),
    (607.90, 633.40, "I don't know how many thousands, how many lakhs of murids will follow their master — think of it — they will be in crores. Qadeer Piya had lakhs of murids; now his murids have lakhs of murids. MashaAllah. Where the master will be, the murids will be too, InshaAllah."),
    (634.79, 687.22, "What is khilafat? Now listen. Everyone thinks it is a fine thing to have khilafat, but it is a great thing — it comes from above. One has to think: am I worthy of it? Do I have that station, that connection with Allah and His Messenger ﷺ? He may think it, but he should not ask; he should stay silent. Allah gives what He wills."),
    (689.60, 715.06, "When we ask once, Allah does not give; even twice, He does not. The third time it comes sternly: “I am telling you — you are to give him khilafat, and you are not giving it?” “Give it to him.” “Yes, sir.” And he gave it. MashaAllah."),
    (717.20, 736.74, "So what is khilafat? It is the confirmation that a murid has become worthy."),
    (738.40, 776.16, "Students study; by studying they become qualified, and the teacher gives them a certificate — the government gives a certificate."),
    (778.40, 815.70, "But remember: neither a merely formal discipleship is of any use, nor a merely formal khilafat. In many places khilafat is given to whoever they like. Some people come and say, “Give me khilafat” — many say it to me. A'udhu billah!"),
    (817.52, 845.66, "Faith and good deeds — both are a gift from Allah."),
    (879.76, 909.90, "I always keep telling people. I am reading the translation of the verse of Surah an-Nisa: “If, when they had wronged themselves, they had come to you and asked forgiveness of Allah, and the Messenger had asked forgiveness for them,”"),
    (911.82, 920.06, "'…they would have found Allah Accepting of repentance, Most Merciful.”"),
    (921.62, 929.62, "MashaAllah. Now, this is page seven. Bismillah."),
    (930.50, 936.92, "So what, after all, is a khalifa?"),
    (937.88, 945.90, "“Khalifa” comes from “khalaf” — and khalaf means “behind”, “what comes after”."),
    (946.78, 961.70, "The one who follows the one before him and carries on his work is his khalifa — his successor."),
    (962.34, 976.42, "From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the Muslims received the Qur'an and the hadith, and through the blessing of his company their selves were purified — our nafs became pure."),
    (977.48, 981.92, "Tazkiya-e-nafs means the purifying of our self."),
    (982.78, 1002.52, "Whoever recites the Holy Qur'an to people and teaches others to read it correctly — that is, the qari — he too is a khalifa."),
    (1003.62, 1011.70, "Whoever explains the meanings of the Holy Qur'an — that is, writes tafsir — is a mufassir: a khalifa."),
    (1013.10, 1022.64, "Whoever narrates the hadith of the Prophet ﷺ and, after verifying them, passes them on to the Ummah — that is, the muhaddith — he too is a khalifa."),
    (1023.92, 1041.82, "Whoever derives rulings from the Qur'an and hadith — draws them out in the light of the Qur'an and hadith: “this is the ruling” —"),
    (1043.38, 1056.96, "that is, the mujtahid and the faqih — he too is a khalifa."),
    (1057.06, 1081.94, "A faqih, you see, takes the verses of the Qur'an and the hadith related to them and says: we should act according to fiqh. That is fiqh, and the one who does it is the faqih — the mujtahid and faqih; he too is a khalifa."),
    (1082.74, 1095.12, "Whoever keeps people on correct beliefs and answers the enemies of Islam — that is, the mutakallim — he too is a khalifa."),
    (1096.42, 1107.16, "[reads it again] Whoever keeps people on correct beliefs and answers the enemies of Islam — the mutakallim — he too is a khalifa."),
    (1109.04, 1132.08, "In his later years, outward government and rule also came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So a just king who follows the Shari'ah and makes others keep to the laws of Islam — he too is a khalifa."),
    (1133.60, 1140.32, "He is a king, but he too becomes a khalifa: he walks on Islam and makes the people keep to it."),
    (1140.68, 1185.82, "Whoever explains the secrets of the deen — the deen has secrets, hidden things that cannot be grasped outwardly, and he explains those too — whoever purifies the self, corrects the thoughts and teaches spirituality: he too is a khalifa."),
    (1187.86, 1219.70, "[He reads both passages again: the just king, and the one who teaches the secrets of the deen and spirituality.]"),
    (1220.34, 1222.38, "And he is the better khalifa."),
    (1228.08, 1240.22, "Whoever teaches soldiering is also a khalifa. We had training in all of that too — binnot (stick-fighting), wrestling and so on."),
    (1241.42, 1256.88, "In it there was the strike Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to make with his sword — the *zarb-e-Haidari*, as it is called. People could not get it."),
    (1257.64, 1274.26, "A man became Hazrat's murid and came. After a while he said that he did binnot, sword and all these things. “Is that so? Do you know the *zarb-e-Haidari*?” “Yes, I know it.”"),
    (1274.90, 1286.10, "“Then show me.” At once he drew and struck, exactly as it should be done — he showed the zarb-e-Haidari. Oh!"),
    (1287.54, 1300.44, "Then Hazrat said: “In this, you have become *my teacher*. In this, you have become *my teacher*.” That is how it was — the zarb-e-Haidari."),
    (1301.54, 1307.82, "And once it happened that he was showing us how to wrestle and what to do."),
    (1308.10, 1328.18, "And besides that he taught us: when you fight with the stick, with a sword or with a staff, don't look here and there — no — keep looking into the eyes of the one you are fighting. Don't look here and there."),
    (1329.48, 1337.14, "So when we fought, that is what we did: we kept looking at him."),
    (1337.76, 1360.58, "In the same way I tell you: when I say something, open your eyes and look at me — don't sit with your head bowed out of respect, not at all. From my gaze into your gaze, into your eyes, a state will pass from here."),
    (1361.90, 1373.82, "It is the matter of the Qur'an, the hadith, the glory and greatness of the Prophet ﷺ and of the awliya of Allah — and it is going from here into your eyes."),
    (1374.98, 1377.48, "In our times there were many kinds of mashaikh."),
    (1378.02, 1401.50, "In short: the more one follows the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, spreads his teaching and walks in the footsteps of “Balligh ma unzila ilayk”, the more he is a khalifa in that same measure."),
    (1402.36, 1413.80, "“Convey to the people what has been sent down to you.” Balligh — convey; ma unzila — what has been sent down; ilayka — to you."),
    (1415.48, 1427.30, "Whoever, from beginning to end, in all his work serves the mission of the Prophet — what can be said of him! He is the successor of the Prophet ﷺ, the very image of Muhammad ﷺ —"),
    (1428.98, 1437.10, "like Hazrat Abu Bakr Siddiq, Hazrat Umar Farooq, Hazrat Usman Ghani and Hazrat Ali Murtaza, may Allah be pleased with them."),
    (1614.68, 1627.26, "In those days there was no call for public donations, nor any need for orphanages. The murids did not neglect serving their master, and the master did not neglect the upbringing and training of his murids."),
    (1629.60, 1639.90, "Now the times have changed: neither that master nor that murid remains. From morning to evening there is a great noise about donations, but no work is seen to be done."),
    (1647.22, 1669.74, "Nowadays donations are collected for widows and orphans. But who are the widows? The wives of the pir sahib himself — the pir is alive, and his wife is the “widow”!"),
    (1670.50, 1681.82, "That is, instead of the widows, the pir gives it to his own wife. And who are the orphans? The pir's own children."),
    (1683.20, 1688.14, "So what is left for me? To weep in my heart and to lament with my tongue."),
    (1689.44, 1694.56, "[A note at the end of the page about contributions to the Siddiqi institute.]"),
]
